<p></p>
<i>
<p></p>
In June 2009, the Financial Accounting Standards Board announced new Financial Accounting Statements No. 166 (FAS 166), &#8220;Accounting for Transfers of Financial Assets," and No. 167 (FAS 167), &#8220;Amendments to FASB Interpretation No. 46(R)," to be implemented by banks as of the beginning of each reporting entity&#8217;s first annual reporting period that begins after November 15, 2009.<sup>2</sup> <b>Questions 25-26</b>
ask about the effects of these new rules on your bank.    </i>
