</td><td align="right" headers="t col2 col2p">
    100.0 
</td><td align="right" headers="t col3">
   20    
</td><td align="right" headers="t col3 col3p">
    100.0 
</td>
</tr>
</table></center>

<ul><ul><p>For this question,   10    respondents answered &#8220;Not applicable to my bank.&#8221;</p></ul></ul>


<hr noshade="noshade" size="1"><a name="fn1"></a>
              1. The sample is selected from among the largest banks in
              each Federal Reserve District. In the table, large banks
              are defined as those with total domestic assets of $20
              billion or more as of    December 31, 2009.    The combined assets
              of the  31  large banks totaled    $6.3 trillion, compared to
                 $6.6 trillion for the entire panel of  56  banks, and $10.4
              trillion for all domestically chartered, federally insured
              commercial banks.
	      <p></p>
	      <a name="fn2"></a>
	      2. For more information on FAS 166 and 167, please see the Financial Accounting Standards Board's news release: <a href="http://www.fasb.org/cs/ContentServer?c=FASBContent_C&pagename=FASB/FASBContent_C/NewsPage&cid=1176156240834">www.fasb.org/cs/ContentServer?c=FASBContent_C&pagename=FASB/FASBContent_C/NewsPage&cid=1176156240834</a>. 
